message: >-
  If you use SENTINEL-X in academic or research work, please cite it using
  the metadata below.
type: software
title: "SENTINEL-X: Federated Reinforcement Learning for Autonomous Spacecraft Fault Detection and Recovery"
authors:
  - family-names: Novais
    given-names: Daniel
    orcid: ""
    affiliation: ""
repository-code: "https://github.com/danielnovais-tech/SENTINEL-X"
url: "https://github.com/danielnovais-tech/SENTINEL-X"
abstract: >-
  SENTINEL-X is an open-source platform for autonomous fault detection,
  isolation, and recovery (FDIR) in spacecraft swarms.  The system combines
  deep reinforcement learning (DRL) with federated model aggregation,
  LTL safety constraints, formal policy verification, TFLite int8 deployment
  on Cortex-M microcontrollers, leader-follower formation control, distributed
  consensus protocols, and adapters for NASA F Prime and ESA TASTE
  mission-control stacks.
keywords:
  - reinforcement-learning
  - spacecraft
  - fault-detection
  - federated-learning
  - embedded-ai
  - space-autonomy
  - formation-flying
  - mission-control
